# rule.always.cure-at-the-owner

> **aim each fix at the file its owner publishes, never at a copy. before an edit, name the owner of the source and whether the edit reaches the next reader.**

| the miss | the cure |
|---|---|
| a local copy of a skill or brief an upstream publishes | a mod, a patch, or a task into the repo of the owner; the copy is no fix |
| a symptom met in one tree | the cause in the shared source; a one-tree grant bridges, never cures |
| a defect in a peer's output | the peer's own tool or role, built by its owner |

step one, before any edit: read where the path resolves (a link to main, a copy, an installed package) and who publishes it.
test: **who publishes this file, and does my edit reach the next reader?**

enforcement: a fix aimed at a copy where an owner publishes the source = **blocker** · a fix with no named owner of its source = **nitpick**.
case: `….example=the-local-copy.md` · argument and sources: the `.md`.
